{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int MAX = 33;\nlong long n, m;\nlong long bin[66];\nstruct matrix {\n    long long d[MAX][MAX];\n    matrix() { memset(d, 0, sizeof(d)); }\n    matrix operator*(const matrix &b) const {\n        matrix c;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n            for (int k = 0; k <= m; ++k)\n                if (d[i][k])\n                    for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j)\n                        c.d[i][j] = (c.d[i][j] + d[i][k] * b.d[k][j]) % MOD;\n        return c;\n    }\n} ans, P[66][MAX], S[66][MAX], A[66][MAX];\nlong long read() {\n    long long x = 0, s = 1;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') { if (c == '-') s = -1; c = getchar(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') { x = x * 10 + c - '0'; c = getchar(); }\n    return x * s;\n}\nsigned main() {\n    n = read(); m = read();\n    int len = 0;\n    long long t = n;\n    do {\n        bin[len++] = t % m;\n        t /= m;\n    } while (t);\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) ans.d[0][i] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j) A[i][0].d[j][j] = 1;\n        if (i == 0) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                A[i][j].d[m][m] = 1;\n                for (int k = 0; k < m; ++k) {\n                    if (k != j) { A[i][j].d[k][k] = 1; continue; }\n                    for (int l = 0; l <= m; ++l) A[i][j].d[k][l] = 1;\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                if (j == 0) A[i][j] = S[i-1][0];\n                else A[i][j] = S[i-1][j] * P[i-1][j-1];\n            }\n        }\n        P[i][0] = A[i][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j) P[i][j] = P[i][j-1] * A[i][j];\n        S[i][m-1] = A[i][m-1];\n        for (int j = m-2; j >= 0; --j) S[i][j] = A[i][j] * S[i][j+1];\n    }\n    int cur = 0;\n    for (int i = len-1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        for (long long cnt = bin[i]; cnt > 0; --cnt) {\n            ans = ans * A[i][cur];\n            ++cur;\n            if (cur == m) cur = 0;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans.d[0][m] << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B):\n    n = len(A)\n    C = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        for k in range(n):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(n):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef vec_mul(vec, mat):\n    n = len(vec)\n    res = [0] * n\n    for j in range(n):\n        s = 0\n        for k in range(n):\n            s = (s + vec[k] * mat[k][j]) % MOD\n        res[j] = s\n    return res\n\ndef identity(n):\n    return [[1 if i == j else 0 for j in range(n)] for i in range(n)]\n\ndef zero(n):\n    return [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\ndef copy_mat(mat):\n    return [row[:] for row in mat]\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\n\n# get digits in base m (least significant first)\nbin_digits = []\nif n == 0:\n    bin_digits = [0]\nelse:\n    t = n\n    while t > 0:\n        bin_digits.append(t % m)\n        t //= m\nlen_digits = len(bin_digits)\n\n# initial ans as row vector of ones\nans = [1] * (m + 1)\n\n# allocate lists for A, P, S\nA = [[None] * m for _ in range(len_digits)]\nP = [[None] * m for _ in range(len_digits)]\nS = [[None] * m for _ in range(len_digits)]\n\nfor i in range(len_digits):\n    # set A[i][0] to identity first (will be overwritten for i==0)\n    A[i][0] = identity(m + 1)\n    if i == 0:\n        for j in range(m):\n            mat = zero(m + 1)\n            mat[m][m] = 1\n            for k in range(m):\n                if k != j:\n                    mat[k][k] = 1\n                else:\n                    for l in range(m + 1):\n                        mat[k][l] = 1\n            A[i][j] = mat\n    else:\n        for j in range(m):\n            if j == 0:\n                A[i][j] = copy_mat(S[i - 1][0])\n            else:\n                A[i][j] = mat_mul(S[i - 1][j], P[i - 1][j - 1])\n    # compute P[i]\n    P[i][0] = copy_mat(A[i][0])\n    for j in range(1, m):\n        P[i][j] = mat_mul(P[i][j - 1], A[i][j])\n    # compute S[i]\n    S[i][m - 1] = copy_mat(A[i][m - 1])\n    for j in range(m - 2, -1, -1):\n        S[i][j] = mat_mul(A[i][j], S[i][j + 1])\n\ncur = 0\nfor i in range(len_digits - 1, -1, -1):\n    cnt = bin_digits[i]\n    while cnt > 0:\n        ans = vec_mul(ans, A[i][cur])\n        cur += 1\n        if cur == m:\n            cur = 0\n        cnt -= 1\n\nprint(ans[m])\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.0002675890573300421, -0.16208356618881226, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -1.311301275563892e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.006728847976773977, -6.139089964563027e-05, -0.002200088929384947, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.3470558769768104e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -1.418580